.context BLBX
This model passes the feed through to the tailing. A water stream can be connected directly to the unit. This model can be changed using the software development kit to suit your needs.
.context NAGE
This model was developed at the Julius Kruttschnitt Mineral Research Centre and is an extension of the original model for the performance of the hydrocyclone that was developed by Lynch and Rao. This model was developed by multilinear regression of experimental data that was obtained from tests on several Krebs cyclones. the model consists of empirical relationships for predicting the corrected D50, the flow through the hydrocyclone as a function of the pressure drop and the fractional recovery of the water. The exponential sum model is used for the partition function. The model, as presented by the authors, also includes an empirical expression for the prediction of the fractional recovery by volume of total feed to the underflow.  However this makes the model internally inconsistent and the later relationship is not used in the simulation of performance of the unit. It is used only to return the extent of the inconsistency in the report file.

Parameters:
  Calibration factor for D50c   KD0
  Calibration factor for total slurry flowrate    KQ0
  Calibration factor for water recovery to underflow    KW1
  Efficiency factor
  Diameter of cyclindrical section
  Inlet diameter (diameter of circle of same area as cyclone inlet)
  Overflow (vortex finder) diameter
  Underflow (apex) diameter
  Length of cylindrical section
  Cone full angle (degrees)


.context CBOX
This model is a splitter. It is written in C and can be used as a simple profile for users model subroutines that are written in C.

Parameters:
  Splitter fraction to tailing
  
